      "note": "2.0.0 (11 Nov 2026, dunes round): the frozen Boulevard-derived sand look (shared/materials/boulevard-ground.js, unchanged; see 1.0.0 for its history) on a generic desert terrain of our own (builder/sculpt/desert-terrain.js, dunes.js): r187 webgpu_tsl_procedural_terrain (noise height field, normals from neighbouring heights) and webgl_geometry_terrain (a height field written once into an indexed grid). Dune types transverse, barchan, star and linear from domain-warped aeolian profiles with the slip face at the slope cap; a flat clear zone round every placed piece from the scene layout (lib/scene/layout.mjs), replacing 1.0.0's fixed flatRadius round the origin; the wet band from every water area (1.0.0's `shore` param); a distance-graded grid (one draw); height-field normals. Boulevard's sand was one flat plane under the whole map (reference/desert-sand.js): the no-loss pixel rule against it is expected to fail for the changed look.",
